.page reimusay 1 let Reimu say something

# SYNOPSIS
*reimusay* [*-nt*] [*-W* _COLUMNS_] [_TEXT_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`reimusay` draws a speech bubble containing _TEXT_ and Reimu Hakurei underneath it. If no text is given on the command line it is read from standard input. The text is wrapped to 40 columns.

# OPTIONS
@ *-W* _COLUMNS_
    Wrap the text at _COLUMNS_ instead of 40.
@ *-n*
    Do not wrap: keep the lines of the input as they are.
@ *-t*
    A thought bubble instead of a speech bubble.

# EXAMPLES
    reimusay "Offerings are welcome."
    fortune -a | reimusay -n
    echo "I am not lazy, I am conserving energy." | reimusay -t

# SEE ALSO
kappasay(1), omikuji(1), saisen(1)
